ely leads to a  series of events that sees them  crapped on the Madonn a seemingly  haunted abandoned ship held captive by a  pirate gang who were convinced that the  ship which is riddled with dead bodies  contains treasure naturally things start  going bump in the night and the gang  finds themselves dealing with various  goals and terrors there are plot holes  and character inconsistencies throughout  some minor some more blatant it's easy  to forgive the questionable presence of  rats all over the boat still knowing on  hunks of meat that have been on the ship  since the 40s but it's less easy to  excuse how PLAs day the characters act  about the horrifying situations they  find themselves in the dialog is  generally not very good either at times  it successfully recreates the feeling of  watching a fun but silly teen slasher  but it can also be annoying when the  five central characters interactions  sounds stilted and unrealistic yeah man  this whole rust buckets one tetanus shot  from the bottom of the ocean we already  tried to escape didn't exactly work out  without spoiling anything the story  explains a little too much about what's  happening on the Madonn in a way that  makes repeated playthroughs much less  satisfying there's also an over-reliance  on jump scares which cheapens the horror  experience on the plus side it looks  tremendous the character models can be a  bit waxy but the ship is extremely  detailed and creepy and the game  effectively communicates how unpleasant  the act of exploring a creaky rust  bucket full of dark corners and rotting  corpses must be  you hear that if by that you mean that  terrifying sound then no I didn't write  you know you did was it something moving  something moving would make that sound  sure the trade-off at least on a bass  ps4 is that the animations frequently  stutter breaking the mood as frames slip  away there are pacing issues too  especially with the extremely slow  opening section that weighs down repea